@baseUrl = http://localhost:5100
@itemId = REPLACE_WITH_ITEM_ID
@version = REPLACE_WITH_LATEST_ITEM_VERSION

### Create a fictional item (only against a disposable database); category 2 is Transport
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/savings-items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Car service example",
  "category": 2,
  "targetAmount": 1000,
  "allocatedAmount": 100,
  "startDate": "2026-01-01",
  "targetDate": "2027-04-01"
}

### Read the current version before editing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/savings-items/{{itemId}}

### Edit name, deadline and category only; refresh the version after every write
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/savings-items/{{itemId}}/details
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Car maintenance example",
  "targetDate": "2027-05-01",
  "category": 2,
  "version": "{{version}}"
}

### Missing category returns 400 (including for uncategorised legacy items)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/savings-items/{{itemId}}/details
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Car service example",
  "targetDate": "2027-04-01",
  "version": "{{version}}"
}

### Editing a missing item returns 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/savings-items/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/details
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Missing example",
  "targetDate": "2027-04-01",
  "category": 2,
  "version": "{{version}}"
}
